        "id": 14416,
        "name": "dshields",
        "username": "dshields",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dshields/{size}/1968_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-08T19:50:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So I want to make sure we followed the rules correctly.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>We were playing in Freedom Tower Map, Wraith Pops into Level 3 With---</p><p><strong>Slip into shadows</strong>: The first time the wraith would be attacked each turn, she may sprint. Then resolve that attack. (If the attack is now impossible, the attack misses.)</p><p>Ra is at her 2 O clock With--</p><p><strong>Blazing Tornado</strong> at her 5 O Clock.</p><p><strong>Living Pyre:</strong> Ra Generates Hazard Spaces.</p><p>The Operative is at her 10 O Clock with—</p><p><strong>Hidden Blast Strike:</strong> The Operative Generates Hazard Spaces for Enemies.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The book Defines and attack as:</p><p><strong>ATTACK: AN ACTION OR ABILITY THAT HAS THE ATTACK DIE CODE.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So we Ruled that The Wraith would sprint one square forward, activating Ra’s and The Operative’s 2<sup>nd</sup> Hazzard Space. Because this is the 2<sup>nd</sup> attack, she has to resolve this, then continue her Sprint forward then resolve the first attack which now misses.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Is this Correct??</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:30.153Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 19,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 95.2,
